
=== print_lore(character) ===
    { character:
        -normie:
            ~ normie_lore()
        -normie2:
            ~ normie_lore()            
        -innocent:
            ~ innocent_lore()
        -hunter:
            ~ hunter_lore()            
        -another_hunter:
            ~ hunter_lore()
        -experienced_hunter:
            ~ hunter_lore()                      
        -thrall:
            ~ thrall_lore()
        -handy_andy:
            ~ handy_andy_lore()         
        -douche:
            ~ douche_lore()
            
        - gym_bro: // MORE JUICE!
            ~ gym_bro_lore()
           
        - cryptid:
            ~ cryptid_lore()
           
        - former_flame:
            ~ former_flame_lore()
        - mortal_lover:
            ~ mortal_lover_lore()
            
        - goth:
            ~ goth_lore()
            
        - ghost:
            ~ ghost_lore()
            
        - cheater:
            ~ cheater_lore()

        - else:
            MISSING            
           
    }
    <> [lore]
    ->->

    
=== function douche_lore()
{~ He's wearing a trucker cap backwards.|His fingers are knotted in a parody handsign.}
<> {~ An arm draped over a very drunk woman.|The fish he's holding has bulging, mad eyes.}
<> {~ His first message is a dick. Presumably his.|He sends you the eggplant emoji followed by several sprays of water.}

=== function normie_lore()
{~ Golf shirt and chinos.|Lite beer set in front of a mediocre sunset.}
<> {~ A photo of him mid-golf swing.|Smiling awkwardly in a badly cropped group shot.}
<> A total normie.

=== function cheater_lore()
{~ He doesn't want to meet in public. That suits you fine.|Only in town for a few days. He texts the address of a hotel.} 


=== function hunter_lore()
{~ Buff but his eyes are haunted.| He's not looking for a date, he's looking for revenge.}
<> {~ The red flags you can't ignore.|The message is meant for you.} 

=== function another_hunter_lore()
{~ Buff but his eyes are haunted.| He's not looking for a date, he's looking for revenge.}
<> {~ The red flags you can't ignore.| } 

=== function experienced_hunter_lore()
{~ Buff but his eyes are haunted.| He's not looking for a date, he's looking for revenge.}
<> {~ The red flags you can't ignore.| } 

=== function innocent_lore()
{~ They have kind eyes. Too kind to survive in a world this cruel. Would it be kindness to spare them?|In one photo a bird is perched on her finger, she's smiling in pure delight.} 

=== function handy_andy_lore()
{~ Handy with powertools. |Capable of walking in sunlight.| If he didn't have a service kink, he will soon.}
<> You could bend him to your will so easily.

=== function thrall_lore()
Your {~ thrall|pet|emergency blood supply}. Send him to cover your tracks.

=== function gym_bro_lore()
{~ Those thick arms are nice. Especially the engorged veins wrapping them.|He'll taste like whey powder and sweat.} 

=== function ghost_lore()
{~ You know who they were.|A mere echo of life.|Should you feel guilty?}

=== function cryptid_lore()
{~ Its smile is too feral. |Its glittering skin too moist. That's not make up.}

=== function vampire_lore()
{~ A glint of sharp teeth.|Her white skin is too white. She's sipping red wine. Oh... not wine.}

=== function goth_lore()
{~ They're excited to get bitten. You're not sure if they believe it's real or a kink thing.|A skinny body armored with black lace.}

=== function mortal_lover_lore()
{~ They offer you their blood freely.|How can they love a monster like you.|Can you control yourself?|They remind you how to be human.}

=== function former_flame_lore()
{~ You've crossed paths before.|You two had a little fun before it fizzled.}
<> One of you ghosted the other. Now one of you is really going to become a ghost.
